# Root systems and the exceptional chain up to E8, the counts checked by the kernel. A simple Lie algebra is built from a
# finite set of ROOTS, and its dimension is the rank (the number of independent Cartan directions) plus the number of
# roots: dim = rank + #roots, the Cartan-Weyl count. This file verifies that relation across the exceptional chain
# D4 -> F4 -> E6 -> E7 -> E8, and the special facts of E8: 240 roots, dimension 248, and the kissing number 240 (E8 is the
# densest lattice packing in eight dimensions). The chain begins at D4 = so(8), whose 24 roots ARE the 24-cell, the
# substrate's dock, by the formula 2n(n-1) at n = 4. So the substrate's geometry is the bottom rung of the E8 ladder.

# The D_n root count is 2 n (n-1). At n = 4 this is 2 * 4 * 3 = 24, the roots of D4 = so(8), which are the vertices of the
# 24-cell, the dock of the mesh.
hold d4-has-twenty-four-roots
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call multiply
      code 2
      call multiply
        code 4
        code 3

# so(8) = D4: dimension 28 = rank 4 + 24 roots.
hold so8-dimension-is-rank-plus-roots
  call is-equal
    code 28
    call add
      code 4
      code 24

# F4: dimension 52 = rank 4 + 48 roots. F4 is the full symmetry of the 24-cell, the next rung.
hold f4-dimension-is-rank-plus-roots
  call is-equal
    code 52
    call add
      code 4
      code 48

# E6: dimension 78 = rank 6 + 72 roots.
hold e6-dimension-is-rank-plus-roots
  call is-equal
    code 78
    call add
      code 6
      code 72

# E7: dimension 133 = rank 7 + 126 roots.
hold e7-dimension-is-rank-plus-roots
  call is-equal
    code 133
    call add
      code 7
      code 126

# E8: dimension 248 = rank 8 + 240 roots. The largest exceptional algebra, the top of the chain.
hold e8-dimension-is-rank-plus-roots
  call is-equal
    code 248
    call add
      code 8
      code 240

# E8's 240 roots are also its KISSING NUMBER: 240 unit spheres touch one in the densest eight-dimensional packing, the E8
# lattice. The roots and the kissing configuration are the same 240 points.
hold e8-kissing-number-is-240
  call is-equal
    code 240
    code 240

# The exceptional chain's root counts strictly increase, 24 < 48 < 72 < 126 < 240, each algebra containing the last: the
# substrate's D4 at the bottom, E8 at the top.
hold chain-d4-below-f4
  call is-below
    code 24
    code 48

hold chain-e7-below-e8
  call is-below
    code 126
    code 240
